      "body": "## Summary\n\nRunning `swift --help` currently raises `KeyError: '--help'` instead of showing top-level help, and running `swift` with no arguments raises `IndexError`. The CLI entry point looks up the first argument directly in `ROUTE_MAPPING` without special-casing help flags.\n\n## Change\n\nIn `cli_main` (swift/cli/main.py), before the routing lookup:\n\n- print `Usage: swift <command> [options]` and the sorted list of available subcommands\n- return successfully when the first argument is missing, `-h` or `--help`\n\nThe routing path for real subcommands is unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\nLocal matrix (with heavy deps stubbed):\n\n- `swift --help` → prints usage + 12 commands, exits 0\n- `swift -h` → same\n- `swift` (no args) → same (previously IndexError)\n- `swift sft --model ...` → still routed to `swift.cli.sft` unchanged\n\nFixes #10287",
